   "metadata": {
    "editable": true,
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "### Exercise: categorical plots\n",
    "\n",
    "First, let's set up DataFrames for plotting. We'll use data from the Morton et al. (2013) free-recall study. Participants studied lists of celebrities, locations, and objects, and then were asked to recall the items in any order. Lists were either pure (all the same category) or mixed (items from each of the three categories)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "id": "b6bbf002",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fr = (\n",
    "    pl.read_csv(datasets.get_dataset_file(\"Morton2013\"), null_values=\"n/a\")\n",
    "    .filter(pl.col(\"study\"))\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d90d3a36",
   "metadata": {
    "editable": true,
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "First, we'll get the mean fraction of items recalled for each subject and list type."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "f7e0bdd0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<div><style>\n",
       ".dataframe > thead > tr,\n",
       ".dataframe > tbody > tr {\n",
       "  text-align: right;\n",
       "  white-space: pre-wrap;\n",
       "}\n",
       "</style>\n",
       "<small>shape: (2, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>subject</th><th>list_type</th><th>recall</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>str</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;mixed&quot;</td><td>0.476389</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;pure&quot;</td><td>0.564815</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "shape: (2, 3)\n",
       "┌─────────┬───────────┬──────────┐\n",
       "│ subject ┆ list_type ┆ recall   │\n",
       "│ ---     ┆ ---       ┆ ---      │\n",
       "│ i64     ┆ str       ┆ f64      │\n",
       "╞═════════╪═══════════╪══════════╡\n",
       "│ 1       ┆ mixed     ┆ 0.476389 │\n",
       "│ 1       ┆ pure      ┆ 0.564815 │\n",
       "└─────────┴───────────┴──────────┘"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 26,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "recall_lt = (\n",
    "    fr.group_by(\"subject\", \"list_type\")\n",
    "    .agg(pl.col(\"recall\").mean())\n",
    "    .sort(\"subject\", \"list_type\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "recall_lt.head(2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "61d6221f",
   "metadata": {
    "editable": true,
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Next, we'll split things up a little more, to get the mean fraction of items recalled for each subject, list type, and category."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "79e32fc6",
   "metadata": {
    "editable": true,
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": ""
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<div><style>\n",
       ".dataframe > thead > tr,\n",
       ".dataframe > tbody > tr {\n",
       "  text-align: right;\n",
       "  white-space: pre-wrap;\n",
       "}\n",
       "</style>\n",
       "<small>shape: (6, 4)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>subject</th><th>list_type</th><th>category</th><th>recall</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;mixed&quot;</td><td>&quot;cel&quot;</td><td>0.5875</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;mixed&quot;</td><td>&quot;loc&quot;</td><td>0.433333</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;mixed&quot;</td><td>&quot;obj&quot;</td><td>0.408333</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;pure&quot;</td><td>&quot;cel&quot;</td><td>0.625</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;pure&quot;</td><td>&quot;loc&quot;</td><td>0.5625</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;pure&quot;</td><td>&quot;obj&quot;</td><td>0.506944</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
